{
  "_comment": [
    "ECS task definition for rithm-api. Replace <ACCOUNT>, <SECRET_RDS_ARN>,",
    "<SECRET_APP_ARN>, <SHA>, <JOBS_QUEUE_URL>, <TOPIC_ARN>, <ASSETS_BUCKET>,",
    "<ANAM_VOICE_ID>",
    "and <ESTIMATED_COLD_START_SECONDS> before registering.",
    "",
    "THREE THINGS THAT WILL BITE, in the order they will bite you:",
    "",
    "1. Every secret ARN needs the TRAILING '::'. The syntax is",
    "   <arn>:<json-key>:<version-stage>:<version-id>; omit the two empty",
    "   trailing fields and ECS injects the entire JSON blob as the value.",
    "",
    "2. ASSETS_BUCKET is a bucket NAME, not an ARN. presign_get passes it",
    "   straight to boto3's Bucket= parameter, so an 'arn:aws:s3:::...' value",
    "   yields presigned URLs that do not resolve — and that surfaces at the",
    "   'does the track actually play' gate, not at deploy time.",
    "",
    "3. SSE_TOKEN_SECRET, not SSE_SIGNING_KEY. Settings uses extra='ignore',",
    "   so a misspelled name does not error — it silently falls back to the",
    "   default that is published in this repo. main.py's lifespan refuses to",
    "   boot in prod when that happens, so the symptom is a deployment that",
    "   never stabilises rather than an obviously wrong value.",
    "",
    "4. BEDROCK_LYRICS_MODEL_ID is Nova 2 Lite, NOT Haiku 4.5, and that is",
    "   temporary. Anthropic models on Bedrock are gated behind a one-time",
    "   per-account 'use case details' form; until it is submitted every",
    "   Anthropic id returns ResourceNotFoundException and lyrics degrade to",
    "   ACE-Step. Nova 2 Lite needs no form, answers in ~2.3s (median of 5),",
    "   and produces correctly tagged lyrics. Gemma 3 27B was measured too and",
    "   REJECTED: it exceeds the 10s client read timeout on repeat calls, so it",
    "   cannot sit in front of a 202. Once the form clears, set this back to",
    "   us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0 -- which is still the",
    "   Settings default, so deleting this entry also works.",
    "",
    "5. The `us.` prefix is LOAD-BEARING on both ids. Haiku 4.5 and Nova 2 Lite",
    "   have no plain on-demand foundation-model id, and invoking a bare one",
    "   returns a ValidationException that reads like a typo.",
    "   rithm-api-task-role must also carry the inline",
    "   policy in ops/iam/ -- and it must grant BOTH the profile ARN and the",
    "   regional model ARNs, or a cross-region route 403s intermittently.",
    "   BEDROCK_ENABLED absent or false is not a failure: the API degrades to",
    "   prompt-derived titles and lets ACE-Step write its own lyrics.",
    "",
    "6. BEDROCK_CHAT_MODEL_IDS is an ORDERED FALLBACK CHAIN, comma-separated,",
    "   for the chat assistant. Haiku leads because it is the model we want;",
    "   it and gemma both refuse in under a second today (the Anthropic form",
    "   above, and gemma is deliberately NOT in the task role\u0027s Bedrock",
    "   policy), so leading with them costs ~350ms and buys a chain that needs",
    "   no code change the day either is unblocked. Nova 2 Lite therefore",
    "   serves every chat turn, and it is the same value the Settings default",
    "   carries -- this entry exists so the chain is visible in the console,",
    "   not because it overrides anything. DO NOT add gemma to the IAM policy",
    "   to \u0027complete\u0027 the chain: it stops failing fast and burns its",
    "   full read timeout on every turn, which is a 2.5s chat turn becoming a",
    "   13s one for the weakest model of the three.",
    "",
    "   Chat extraction runs on BEDROCK_TITLE_MODEL_ID\u0027s model",
    "   (amazon.nova-micro-v1:0), which is already granted and enabled -- so",
    "   the chat feature needs NO new model access and NO IAM change.",
    "",
    "7. ANAM_LLM_ID must be CUSTOMER_CLIENT_V1, and it is not a model id. It is",
    "   the value that turns Anam\u0027s OWN brain off and leaves speech-to-text",
    "   and text-to-speech on, so that RITHM\u0027s interviewer keeps answering.",
    "   With anything else there the avatar answers with its own model and the",
    "   failure is SILENT: the reply never reaches /chat/messages, the draft",
    "   never moves, and the Chat door shows a transcript with a hole in it.",
    "   main.py refuses to start rather than let that ship -- so the symptom is",
    "   a deployment that never stabilises, the same trade SSE_TOKEN_SECRET",
    "   makes above. ANAM_VOICE_ID is guarded the same way: it has no default,",
    "   because an avatar with the wrong voice is worse than no avatar.",
    "",
    "   ANAM_ENABLED absent or false is not a failure and is the state every",
    "   environment starts in: the AI Assistant panel is bit-for-bit what it",
    "   was before voice existed, and Talk opens the Coming Soon dialog.",
    "   TURN IT ON LAST, as its own revision -- then turning voice off again is",
    "   one more revision rather than a rollback.",
    "",
    "   ONE KEY IS ONE CONCURRENT SESSION on the free tier, product-wide. If",
    "   dev and prod share it, a developer running `npm run dev` locks",
    "   production out for three minutes and the person on the other end reads",
    "   \u0027someone else is talking\u0027 with no idea it was a colleague. Use a",
    "   second Anam account for non-prod, or keep ANAM_ENABLED false outside",
    "   prod. Not deciding is the same as choosing the first failure.",
    "",
    "desiredCount stays at 1: SSE pub/sub is in-process, and a second task",
    "silently loses completion events for streams it does not own.",
    "",
    "SSE_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS must be 1800. The setting now defaults to 1800, but",
    "the running task's env is what wins. At 300 the first generation of a cold",
    "session can outlive its own stream token, and a single reconnect after a",
    "wifi blip 401s permanently — a spinner that never resolves, unreproducible",
    "locally because local has no cold start.",
    "",
    "CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS is deliberately ABSENT. Production is same-origin:",
    "CloudFront serves the SPA at / and proxies /api/* to this ALB, so no",
    "browser ever makes a cross-origin call. Do not add the CloudFront domain",
    "'to be safe' — the setting exists only so `npm run dev` works.",
    "",
    "This template is BOOTSTRAP DOCUMENTATION, not the deploy source.",
    "deploy-api.yml describes the LIVE task definition and patches only the",
    "image, so values tuned in the console (ESTIMATED_COLD_START_SECONDS,",
    "RATE_LIMIT_PER_24H, SSE_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS) survive every deploy."
  ],
  "family": "rithm-api",
  "networkMode": "awsvpc",
  "requiresCompatibilities": ["FARGATE"],
  "cpu": "512",
  "memory": "1024",
  "executionRoleArn": "arn:aws:iam::<ACCOUNT>:role/ecsTaskExecutionRole",
  "taskRoleArn": "arn:aws:iam::<ACCOUNT>:role/rithm-api-task-role",
  "containerDefinitions": [
    {
      "name": "api",
      "image": "<ACCOUNT>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/rithm/api:<SHA>",
      "essential": true,
      "portMappings": [{ "containerPort": 8080, "protocol": "tcp" }],
      "environment": [
        { "name": "ENVIRONMENT", "value": "prod" },
        { "name": "DB_REQUIRE_SSL", "value": "true" },
        { "name": "LOG_LEVEL", "value": "INFO" },
        { "name": "AWS_REGION", "value": "us-east-1" },
        { "name": "SQS_JOBS_QUEUE_URL", "value": "<JOBS_QUEUE_URL>" },
        { "name": "SNS_COMPLETIONS_TOPIC_ARN", "value": "<TOPIC_ARN>" },
        { "name": "ASSETS_BUCKET", "value": "<ASSETS_BUCKET>" },
        { "name": "RATE_LIMIT_PER_24H", "value": "20" },
        { "name": "MAX_LENGTH_SECONDS", "value": "180" },
        { "name": "SSE_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS", "value": "1800" },
        { "name": "SWEEPER_ENABLED", "value": "true" },
        { "name": "SWEEPER_INTERVAL_SECONDS", "value": "300" },
        { "name": "STUCK_RUNNING_SECONDS", "value": "600" },
        { "name": "STUCK_QUEUED_SECONDS", "value": "1800" },
        { "name": "BEDROCK_ENABLED", "value": "true" },
        { "name": "BEDROCK_LYRICS_MODEL_ID", "value": "us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0" },
        { "name": "BEDROCK_TITLE_MODEL_ID", "value": "amazon.nova-micro-v1:0" },
        {
          "name": "BEDROCK_CHAT_MODEL_IDS",
          "value": "us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0,google.gemma-3-27b-it,us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0"
        },
        {
          "name": "ESTIMATED_COLD_START_SECONDS",
          "value": "<ESTIMATED_COLD_START_SECONDS>"
        },
        { "name": "ANAM_ENABLED", "value": "false" },
        { "name": "ANAM_LLM_ID", "value": "CUSTOMER_CLIENT_V1" },
        { "name": "ANAM_VOICE_ID", "value": "<ANAM_VOICE_ID>" },
        { "name": "ANAM_AVATAR_ID", "value": "3fff7cca-95a6-4980-b478-43488becdfaf" },
        { "name": "ANAM_SESSION_SECONDS", "value": "180" },
        { "name": "ANAM_MAX_SESSIONS_PER_USER_PER_DAY", "value": "10" }
      ],
      "_comment_dev_endpoints": [
        "RITHM_DEV_ENDPOINTS is deliberately ABSENT, not set to '0'.",
        "It mounts POST /internal/dev/enqueue-test-job, which takes no auth and skips",
        "the rate limiter by design (generation/api.py:452) so gates could be driven",
        "repeatedly. The route is kept off CloudFront, but the ALB DNS is public --",
        "so with it on, anyone who finds the ALB can spend GPU budget.",
        "Removed on Day 5. The guard is at router registration (main.py:146), so",
        "absence genuinely unmounts the route: it 404s rather than 403s.",
        "",
        "NOTE: deploy-api.yml describe-and-patches the LIVE task definition and does",
        "not render this template, so editing this file changes nothing in production.",
        "The real removal is a new rithm-api revision -- day-5-spec.md A4."
      ],
      "secrets": [
        {
          "name": "DB_IDENTITY_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ARN>:identity_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "DB_CATALOG_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ARN>:catalog_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "DB_GENERATION_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ARN>:generation_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "DB_CONVERSATION_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ARN>:conversation_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "DB_PERSONALIZATION_DSN",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ARN>:personalization_dsn::"
        },
        {
          "name": "SSE_TOKEN_SECRET",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_APP_ARN>:sse_signing_key::"
        },
        {
          "name": "ANAM_API_KEY",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_APP_ARN>:anam_api_key::"
        }
      ],
      "healthCheck": {
        "command": [
          "CMD-SHELL",
          "curl -fsS http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1"
        ],
        "interval": 30,
        "timeout": 5,
        "retries": 3,
        "startPeriod": 30
      },
      "logConfiguration": {
        "logDriver": "awslogs",
        "options": {
          "awslogs-group": "/ecs/rithm-api",
          "awslogs-region": "us-east-1",
          "awslogs-stream-prefix": "api",
          "awslogs-create-group": "true"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
